//? Title: The Difference Map: Decode the Cross-Projections, Not the Iterate
//? Subtitle: Actual four-call traces, a repaired solution decoder, and explicit limits of step-based stopping
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given two constraint sets through nearest-point projection routines, we want a
point satisfying both constraints. An iteration can settle at a state outside
either set, so identifying the returned feasible point matters as much as the
update itself. The difference map combines two cross-projections to search
for agreement. We retain the original two-line intersection at (2,2), then
expose a one-dimensional fixed point where the old decoder returned an invalid
answer. The corrected canonical driver returns the actual B-side cross-estimate
and records every intermediate state without rerunning shorter prefixes.
An independent two-line matrix predicts contraction or divergence as the
angle and beta change. Small-beta and disjoint-set controls show why the
preserved numerical stop flag is not a feasibility certificate. Stable norms,
checked callbacks and bounded actual histories make those limits observable.
)

\toc

> Start with the original two intersecting lines

Set A is y=x; set B is y=−x+4. Their intersection is (2,2). The original
start (7,−3) lies on B. With beta=1, the first update reaches (2,2), and the
second observes a zero step. The original result remains solution [2,2], two
iterations and zero final residual. The new trace also exposes the estimate
used to decode the result: after only the first update, the B-side cross-
estimate is still [7,−3]. Reaching a good iterate and evaluating agreement
there are separate operations.

Projection formulas are reusable core functions here, rather than report-local
implementations. A hyperplane normal (1,−1) with offset zero defines A;
normal (1,1) with offset four defines B. The complete program prints actual
cross-estimates and norms from one execution.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/difference_map_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto a=[](const std::vector<double>& x){return dm::algorithms::project_affine_hyperplane(x,{1,-1},0);};
  const auto b=[](const std::vector<double>& x){return dm::algorithms::project_affine_hyperplane(x,{1,1},4);};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::difference_map_trace(a,b,{7,-3},1,10000,1e-13);
  const auto r=dm::algorithms::difference_map(a,b,{7,-3},1,10000,1e-13);
  if(t.steps.size()!=2 || r.solution!=std::vector<double>{2,2} || r.solution!=t.result.solution || !r.converged)return 1;
  const auto& first=t.steps.front();const auto& last=t.steps.back();
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(65,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=3.3;box.height=1.9;box.font_size=20;
  d.node("input",{0,0},std::format("x0 = {}\nA(x0) = {}\nB(x0) = {}",first.x_before,first.projection_a,first.projection_b),box)
   .node("cross",{5.3,0},std::format("A(fB) = {}\nB(fA) = {}\nx1 = {}",first.estimate_a,first.estimate_b,first.x_after),box);
  box.fill={220,252,231};d.node("agree",{10.6,0},std::format("Next gap = {:.0f}\nDecoded = {}\nTwo updates",last.gap_norm,t.result.solution),box)
   .edge("input","cross").edge("cross","agree")
   .text({5.3,2.2},"Original affine lines: the iterate reaches (2,2), then agreement is tested",22)
   .text({5.3,-2.1},"Four projection calls per update; return the last B-side cross-estimate",21)
   .save_svg("build/difference_map_original.svg");
  std::print("Original result: solution {}; iterations {}; final step {:.6f}; numerical stop {}.\n\n",r.solution,r.iterations,r.residual,r.converged);
  std::print("| update | x before | A(fB) | B(fA) | x after | step norm | cross gap |\n| ---: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(const auto& s:t.steps)std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} | {:.6f} |\n",s.iteration,s.x_before,s.estimate_a,s.estimate_b,s.x_after,s.step_norm,s.gap_norm);
  std::print("\nFirst relaxed vectors: fA {}; fB {}. Actual A calls {}; B calls {}; coordinate updates {}; retained history entries {}.\n",first.f_a,first.f_b,t.work.projection_a_calls,t.work.projection_b_calls,t.work.coordinate_updates,t.work.history_entries);
}
