> Derive a checkable two-line rate

Now let A be the horizontal axis and B the line through the origin with slope
m>0. Write c=1/√(1+m²), s=m/√(1+m²), so P_A=diag(1,0) and
P_B has rows (c²,cs) and (cs,s²). Substituting these matrices into the
update cancels the reciprocal-beta terms and gives

$$
D_\beta(x)=T_\beta x,\qquad
T_\beta=\begin{pmatrix}c^2&\beta cs\\-\beta cs&c^2\end{pmatrix},\qquad
\|T_\beta x\|=q\|x\|,\quad q=\sqrt{c^4+\beta^2c^2s^2}.
$$
\alttext(The linear difference-map matrix has c squared on its diagonal and plus or minus beta c s off the diagonal. Its Euclidean norm multiplier is the square root of c to the fourth plus beta squared c squared s squared.)

The last equality follows from T_beta transpose times T_beta=q²I. For
beta=1, q=c: shallow crossing angles contract slowly, and perpendicular lines
have q=0. For slope one, beta four instead gives q=√4.25>1 even though both
sets are convex and intersect at the origin. An arbitrary nonzero beta does
not inherit a general convergence claim. The programs deliberately use tol=0
to keep twelve actual updates for these finite comparisons.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/difference_map_rates.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::pair<double,double>> cases{{.25,1},{1,1},{4,1},{1,4}};
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{37,99,235},{234,88,12},{124,58,237}};
  auto angles=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(),beta_plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();double max_relative=0;
  std::print("| slope m | beta | predicted q | updates | final iterate norm | final step | A calls | B calls | history entries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t k=0;k<cases.size();++k) {
    const auto [m,beta]=cases[k];const auto a=[](const std::vector<double>& x){return dm::algorithms::project_affine_hyperplane(x,{0,1},0);};
    const auto b=[m](const std::vector<double>& x){return dm::algorithms::project_affine_hyperplane(x,{-m,1},0);};
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::difference_map_trace(a,b,{3,4},beta,12,0);const double c2=1/(1+m*m),cs=m*c2,q=std::sqrt(c2*c2+beta*beta*cs*cs);
    std::vector<double> iterations{0},lognorm{std::log10(5.)};
    for(const auto& step:t.steps) {
      const double norm=std::hypot(step.x_after[0],step.x_after[1]);const double prediction=5*std::pow(q,step.iteration);
      max_relative=std::max(max_relative,std::abs(norm/prediction-1));iterations.push_back(step.iteration);lognorm.push_back(std::log10(norm));
    }
    if(k<3)angles.line(iterations,lognorm,std::format("slope {}",m),colors[k],2);
    if(k==1 || k==3)beta_plot.line(iterations,lognorm,std::format("beta {}",beta),k==1?colors[0]:colors[1],2);
    std::print("| {} | {} | {:.6f} | {} | {:.6e} | {:.6e} | {} | {} | {} |\n",m,beta,q,t.result.iterations,std::hypot(t.final_iterate[0],t.final_iterate[1]),t.result.residual,t.work.projection_a_calls,t.work.projection_b_calls,t.work.history_entries);
  }
  if(max_relative>1e-10)return 1;
  angles.title("Line angle controls beta=1 contraction").x_label("actual completed updates").y_label("log10(iterate norm)").y_limits(-8,4);
  beta_plot.title("An intersecting convex pair can diverge").x_label("actual completed updates").y_label("log10(iterate norm)").y_limits(-3,7);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(angles).add(beta_plot).size(1100,520).title("Actual histories match an independent two-line matrix").fit_panels().save_svg("build/difference_map_rates.svg");
  std::print("\nAll 48 actual iterate norms checked against 5*q^k; maximum relative discrepancy {:.3e}. No residual floors or prefix reruns.\n",max_relative);
}
